contrast_pool_s2026.pt                # 0.8515 solo (-0.0119 vs the calib_dense_hold control, -0.0032 vs its own contrast_dense control), and seat value 0.0000: the honest greedy over the roster peaks at 0.8763/20 seats with or without it, identical to four decimals. Declined on BOTH rulers, which is why this is a decline and not a deferral - contrast_dense is on the roster precisely because it fails the solo ruler and passes the seat one. Re-open by answering the argument: the widened pool refuted the batch-size explanation on measurement (loss 5.859 vs 3.605 at e0, so 96 keys per anchor really were supplied), so a re-open needs a DIFFERENT representation term, not this one with another weight. See experiments/README.md 2026-08-30 and knee-agrj.
swin_supervised_s2026.pt              # 0.8331 solo (CONVERGED at epoch 6; epochs 7-11 declined) and seat value -0.0012 against greedyseat_v1: the roster of 7 scores 0.8763 and this one makes it 0.8751, band [-0.0020, -0.0003], best possible swap -0.0013. Declined despite being the most DECORRELATED member the project owns — nearest-neighbour 0.8346 against seated members' 0.8772-0.9225 — which is the finding in the decline: maximal diversity cannot pay for a 0.020 solo deficit. Re-open by answering the argument, and the answer is already armed: knee-94ec found that block discovery took the longest ModuleList and so opened only layers.2.blocks.12-17, leaving stage 3 (the top of the network, 1024 wide) frozen for the whole run. swin_wholetop (knee-tsiz) re-runs this recipe byte-identical on the fixed discovery. Re-open on THAT number, not on this one.
swin_wholetop_s2026.pt                # 0.8274 solo, CONVERGED (12 of 12 epochs, peak e6, then 0.8228 / 0.8223 / 0.8197 / 0.8186 / 0.8180). It is the re-run of `swin_supervised` byte-identical on the fixed block discovery (knee-94ec), which doubled trainable parameters to 37,869,696 and opened both 1024-wide stage-3 blocks — and it came out 0.0057 BELOW the handicapped run it was built to correct. So the frozen top was not a handicap on this trunk at this rate; it was the right amount of trunk to move, which is what `swin_wholetop.sh` pre-registered under REFUTES before it ran. Declined below the merit level like everything above, and additionally NOT an instrument: `swin_supervised` is the better member on the same ruler AND the entry it would have taken (`kneemri-swinseat`) was retired for `kneemri-vjepaseat`, whose member beats both. The rate correction this result asks for is already armed as `swin_calib_dense` (knee-csxq) at 4e-5; re-open on THAT number, not on this one. See knee-wqfz for the seat rule this failed and experiments/README.md 2026-08-30.
vit_in21k_s2026.pt                    # TRUNCATED at epoch 5 of 12, so 0.7847 is a FLOOR and not this recipe's number — do not quote it as one. Declined on a TRAJECTORY argument rather than on that floor: across the 99 runs in the processed root with ten or more epochs, the gain from epoch 3 to peak is median +0.0215, p90 +0.0383, max +0.0529, and this arm needed +0.0546 from epoch 4 to reach the 0.8393 its own pre-registration set for a seat — more than the largest such gain the project has ever recorded, measured generously from an earlier epoch of a longer run. The second anchor: swin_supervised sat at 0.8192 at epoch 3 and was still declined as too weak, and this run was 0.044 below that at the same epoch. The remaining 7 epochs (2.3h of card) could only separate COSTS from REFUTES, and both close the trunk for seating, so the card went to swin_wholetop instead. The plumbing suspects were cleared BEFORE the read and none fired: GridFit passes interpolate_pos_encoding, normalization=HALF is declared, discovery finds all twelve ViTLayer, every flag landed in the log. Re-open by answering the trajectory argument with an arm whose epoch-3 value sits in the 0.82-0.84 band seat-worthy runs occupy — a different rate or a longer unfreeze — never by re-quoting 0.7847. See experiments/README.md 2026-08-30 and knee-gnzx.
swin_calib_dense_s2026.pt             # 0.8224 solo, CONVERGED (12 of 12, peak e6, then a clean five-epoch decline to 0.8143). It is the rate correction that `swin_wholetop`'s decline deferred to by name — swinbase at 4e-5, the rate DINOv2 prefers, against `swin_supervised`'s 1e-4 — and it lands 0.0107 BELOW the run it was built to correct. So the chain closes: swin_supervised (0.8331) deferred to swin_wholetop for the frozen-top suspect, swin_wholetop (0.8274) deferred to this arm for the rate suspect, and both suspects are now measured and neither was the deficit. Three converged swinbase runs, none above 0.8331, against the +0.017-0.020 a seat at this trunk's correlation costs. NOTE the confound and do not over-read it: this arm also moved --calibrated-targets and the dense band, so it is DIRECTIONAL on rate and not a matched control — what it rules out is "4e-5 rescues this trunk", not "rate is not a lever". The matched question is armed as `swin_open_half` (knee-23wa), which holds the rate at the control's 1e-4 and moves the opened FRACTION instead. Re-open on THAT number, not on this one.
recal_holdannot_s2026.pt              # 0.8515 proxy on report_labels_v2 (`ruler_check`), 0.9037 gold over the 58 annotated studies. DECLINED AS A MEMBER AND KEPT AS AN INSTRUMENT, which is why this line is long. As a seat it is 0.012 under `calib_dense_hold` at the 224 corner and nothing recommends it. What it established is the arm's own LANDS branch (knee-8wa0): the v3 supervision table — each reader level replaced by its measured positive rate — moves the gold ruler +0.0105 over its matched control at no cost on the proxy, so v3 is the better table to build future label-side members on. DO NOT QUOTE 0.8964 from its training log: the arm passed --labels v3 with --eval-labels unset, so its holdout truth was binarised against the RE-MAPPED values and the ruler moved with the arm; `run_comparison` refuses the pair outright. Re-open as a member only if the dense-corner replication of v3 (ledger follow-up 2) produces one worth seating — never on the gold number, which is n=58 and is a level rather than a selector.

# Added 2026-08-31 00:49Z. The warm-restart lane, both members, declined together because the argument
# against them is one argument. A restart from a converged parent is a TIME mechanism with no quality
# term - now measured on two different trunks from opposite directions - so neither member is worth a
# seat on its own score, and the lane's value is that it reaches a given score faster, not higher.
warm_calib_lowlr_s2026      # Restarted from a converged parent at a reduced rate and did not recover the
                            # parent's peak. The first point of the warm lane's no-quality-term reading.
cnx_warm_anneal_s2026       # 0.8142 peak at epoch 2 of 6, against a parent peak of 0.8186 - inside the
                            # CONVERGED band, not directional. The SHAPE carries it: loss fell monotonically
                            # 0.4636 -> 0.4172 while holdout AUC fell every epoch after the second, and the
                            # one_cycle anneal at epoch 5 produced the run's WORST number (0.8068). The
                            # restart opened 0.0045 BELOW its parent and never recovered; a rate artefact
                            # would have reversed in the anneal. convergence_check reads it clean (six
                            # asked, six recorded), so 0.8142 is a peak and not a floor. Re-open this by
                            # answering the mechanism, never by re-quoting a number.

# Added 2026-08-31 05:30Z. Both arms of the merged-corpus cross, declined together because one argument
# covers them: the corpus lane is one cell wide. Each moved ONE variable off a known-good control, each
# landed INSIDE the paired floor on its own holdout, and each priced at zero as a seat. Neither is a
# refutation of its mechanism - both are reads that the mechanism is already spent where it was applied.
merged_distill_cf.pt        # 0.8637 solo, peak epoch 8 of 12, CONVERGED (epochs 9-11 flat at 0.8636 /
                            # 0.8626 / 0.8627). One variable off `stack_increments_s2026` (0.8642): the
                            # corpus, blend_three_v1 -> merged_blend_v1, with the distill teacher, the
                            # band, the pooling, the rate and `--hold-annotations` all held. Delta
                            # -0.0005, INSIDE the 0.0062 paired floor, so its pre-registration's own
                            # middle branch applies: keep if and only if greedy over the roster picks it.
                            # Greedy priced it +0.0000 (band [-0.0005, +0.0006], best possible swap
                            # +0.0001), so it does not. The arm's value is the ANSWER, not the member:
                            # the merged corpus does not add to a distilled member, which is the third
                            # time a better-labelled signal has failed to compose with a finer one
                            # (merged_dense_cf -0.0028, merged_labelwise_cf below). Re-open only with a
                            # genuinely different external corpus (MRNet, knee-ombx), never with another
                            # cross of the two corpora already here.
merged_labelwise_cf.pt      # 0.8587 solo, peak epoch 9 of 12, CONVERGED. One variable off
                            # `labelwise_dense_s2026` (0.8613): the corpus again. Delta -0.0026, inside
                            # the floor. Seat value +0.0005, band [-0.0002, +0.0012], best possible swap
                            # +0.0005 - all under the +0.0015 this ruler has never been shown to resolve.
                            # DECLINED DESPITE BEING THE MOST DECODE-DIVERSE CANDIDATE EVER PRICED HERE:
                            # nearest-neighbour 0.8873 and mean 0.8583 against a seated spread of
                            # 0.8772-0.9225. That is the finding in the decline, and it is the same sign
                            # the board returned on the architecture axis the same week (vjepaseat_v1
                            # 0.943 against 0.944 with the most distant member the project owns).
                            # Distance without solo strength does not buy a seat - now on two rulers and
                            # two axes. Re-open on a member that is BOTH distant and at or above the
                            # seated quality level, never on a distance number alone.

cover_labelwise_s2026       # 0.8495 solo, seat value -0.0001 against honest12 [-0.0006, +0.0004], best
                            # available swap -0.0000: zero of one clears +0.0015. It reads DISTINCT on the
                            # three-ruler join (rank 0.8587 / js 0.0173 / maha 4.627 against roster
                            # boundaries 0.8956 / 0.0150 / 4.436), which is exactly why the decline is
                            # written rather than assumed: DISTINCT is NECESSARY for a seat and never
                            # sufficient, and a member off the pool's span with nothing to sell is the
                            # shape the join exists to make visible. Its one real content is MCL +0.0247,
                            # starred against both of its controls and given back by six other labels.
                            # Re-open only on a per-finding build that keeps the MCL gain without paying
                            # for it elsewhere - never on the DISTINCT cell alone.

stack224_s2026              # 0.8476 solo against native224's 0.8502, and the axis it belonged to is
                            # CLOSED (knee-qphd, 2026-08-31): full 36-slice coverage is refuted as a member
                            # lever, on cover_labelwise's pre-registered branch. Kept in writing rather
                            # than deleted because its per-label shape is the evidence - a two-label
                            # collapse (Lateral Meniscus -0.0263, Fracture -0.0180) inside a nine-label
                            # rise, which is what named the aggregator mechanism at all. Re-open only if
